   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 329 of the laws of 2015 amending the vehicle and traffic law relating to the residential parking system in the village of Dobbs Ferry in the county of Westchester, in relation to making such provisions permanent",
    "basePrintNo": "S4418",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4418-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 329 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4418\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 329 of the laws of 2015\namending the vehicle and traffic law relating to the residential\nparking system in the village of Dobbs Ferry in the county of\nWestchester, in relation to making such provisions permanent\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nExtends the Village of Dobbs Ferry residential parking permit system\npermanently.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends Section 3 of Chapter 329 of the laws of 2015 by\nextending the Residential parking system in the village of Dobbs Ferry\npermanently.\n\nSection 2 states that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis would extend the sunset date of the Village of Dobbs Ferry\nresidential parking permit program permanently to continue the\nprogram's success in alleviating parking problems for Dobbs Ferry\nresidents located in the area near the Dobbs Ferry train station. The\nVillage of Dobbs Ferry encompasses approximately 3 miles, has over\n11,000 residents and within its boundaries a railroad station\nmaintained and operated by the MTA. The station attracts a large\nnumber of commuters and travelers from outside the village resulting\nin significant traffic and congestion. The residential neighborhood\nadjoining the station lacks sufficient off-street parking and the\nextension of the residential parking permit system will continue to\nalleviate the traffic burden for nearby residents.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nAmends Section 3 of chapter 329 of the laws of 2015\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to State\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
