    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 329 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4418A               REVISED MEMO 06/02/2017\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 329 of the laws of 2015\namending the vehicle and traffic law relating to the residential\nparking system in the village of Dobbs Ferry in the county of\nWestchester, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nExtends the Village of Dobbs Ferry residential parking permit system\nuntil January 1, 2021\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends Section 3 of Chapter 329 of the laws of 2015 by\nextending the Residential parking system in the village of Dobbs Ferry\nuntil January 1, 2021.\n\nSection 2 states that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe legislation extends the Village of Dobbs Ferry residential parking\npermit program to January 1, 2021. The program has been successful in\nalleviating parking problems for Dobbs Ferry residents located in the\narea near the Dobbs Ferry train station. The Village of Dobbs Ferry\nencompasses approximately 3 miles, has over 11,000 residents and\nwithin its boundaries a railroad station maintained and operated by\nthe MTA. The station attracts a large number of commuters and\ntravelers from outside the village resulting in significant traffic\nand congestion. The residential neighborhood adjoining the station\nlacks sufficient off-street parking and the extension of the\nresidential parking permit system for three years will continue to\nalleviate the traffic burden for nearby residents.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nAmends Section 3 of chapter 329 of the laws of 2015\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to State\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
